@a53
define position ("") :: {"argumentdefaults":["",""]} :: warp
if <(size) > ["100"]> then
  switch costume to [Filler \(Size\) v]
else
  switch costume to [Screen v]
end
set size to ((clone Z) * (🎥 Z)) %
switch costume to [Filler \(Movement\) v]
point in direction ((clone Dir) - ((🎥 Dir) + (ShakeDir)))
go to x: (((((clone X) + ((🎥 X) + (ShakeX))) * (🎥 Z)) * ([cos v] of ((🎥 Dir) + (ShakeDir)))) - ((((clone Y) + ((🎥 Y) + (ShakeY))) * (🎥 Z)) * ([sin v] of ((🎥 Dir) + (ShakeDir))))) y: (((((clone X) + ((🎥 X) + (ShakeX))) * (🎥 Z)) * ([sin v] of ((🎥 Dir) + (ShakeDir)))) + ((((clone Y) + ((🎥 Y) + (ShakeY))) * (🎥 Z)) * ([cos v] of ((🎥 Dir) + (ShakeDir))))) // [c1] This is the block that positions the clones. It uses some trigonometry, and I dont fully understand how it works, but you can view some of @MathMathMath's tutorials for more info
switch costume to (:: args)

